x86_64-linux  One clang-only name, `_ZTT1D`: the VTT, which clang emits for a class with a virtual base and cxx1 does not. Nothing wants it until a virtual function is called from inside a base constructor - the one thing a construction vtable exists to make right - and this compiler refuses that shape rather than emitting a table it has not measured. The feature's own remainder, recorded when the virtual base landed and set out at length in virtual-base-diamond.nonames. Every name cxx1 does emit agrees with clang, the vtable and the vbase_offset this case reads through included.
arm64-darwin  The same one name with Mach-O's leading underscore, `__ZTT1D`, for the same reason.
